WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
when working with documents it is

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:06.000
important that the content is structured

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.580
effectively windows has a number of

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.450
tools that allow you to do this and what

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.340
we're going to be looking at in this

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.740
video is the tools that you can find on

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.660
the layout tab so if we click on the

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.850
Layout tab as you can see there are

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.480
three sections here now we're primarily

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:24.560
going to focus on the first two which is

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:27.570
margins page orientation size columns

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:31.830
bricks and the way you can indent and

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:32.880
space the paragraphs around one of the

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.940
tools that were going to look at first

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.820
is the widows and orphans as you can see

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:44.850
it's on kicked here by default this will

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:47.489
be kicked in your windows program if the

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:50.039
widow is an orphans box isn't ticked as

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:51.780
you can see when I start pressing the

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:55.680
enter key and wolven text further down

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:57.239
the table and it was on to a new page it

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.010
actually allows the splitting up of

00:00:57.239 --> 00:01:03.510
paragraphs so you can have information

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.670
starting on one lane and not finishing

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:12.810
till the next lane so if I just undo

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:16.200
what I've done there and then I select

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:18.240
the widows and orphans control make sure

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.450
that's ticked and select look here and

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:26.430
then press the Enter key again to kick

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:28.619
the information on in the next page you

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:32.400
will see that it jumps the paragraph it

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:40.040
won't let you have just one line on the

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:42.180
previous page I just don't do that

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:44.460
another feature that you may find useful

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.960
is the ability to keep paragraphs

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:48.200
together on lanes and a paragraph

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.790
together if you click on the paragraph

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:52.110
expansion control there as you can see

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:56.310
I've got keep lanes together

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.990
ticked in that box there what this means

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:01.950
is that when I can't press the Enter key

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:04.229
I move text further down the table when

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:06.270
it moves on to a new page it

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:10.129
automatically moves a whole paragraph so

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.129
it won't let you split a paragraph up

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:19.840
I'll just glue that back the next tool I

00:02:17.299 --> 00:02:22.579
want to look at is the page break tool

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.349
as you can see all the information is on

00:02:22.579 --> 00:02:27.049
one page there but there is a blank

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:29.989
second page but just backspace that and

00:02:27.049 --> 00:02:32.810
not everything is on one page so for

00:02:29.989 --> 00:02:35.239
example I wish to move the information

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:39.079
from this point forward onto you a new

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:39.620
page you go to bricks and select a page

00:02:39.079 --> 00:02:40.909
break

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:45.230
now that automatically moves the

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:47.359
information on the page - now that's

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:50.299
faint but say for example I wanted to

00:02:47.359 --> 00:02:53.299
have this page in landscape format and

00:02:50.299 --> 00:02:54.889
keep this page in portrait form up if I

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:56.629
try that now so the cursor is blinking

00:02:54.889 --> 00:02:59.870
there and change the orientation to

00:02:56.629 --> 00:03:04.220
landscape both pages change to landscape

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:07.159
so I will just undo that what I need to

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:09.859
do here is I need to undo the pH brick

00:03:07.159 --> 00:03:12.349
that was inserted and Roland said a page

00:03:09.859 --> 00:03:16.639
break I need to insert a section break

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:20.180
next page what this does it again moves

00:03:16.639 --> 00:03:22.159
the information on the page too but this

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.049
allows me to format this page in any way

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:26.750
I want so I can now select the

00:03:24.049 --> 00:03:30.139
orientation and landscape and it will

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:32.060
only change that page as you can see if

00:03:30.139 --> 00:03:33.799
I go to the Home tab and use the fuel

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.019
and hide button to see the formatting

00:03:33.799 --> 00:03:38.540
that is being applied as you can see

00:03:36.019 --> 00:03:40.159
that as a section brick next page so

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:41.659
that has basically moved everything down

00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:44.209
and the formatting that's applied to

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:47.870
that the layout of that page can be

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:54.849
different to pH one if I remove this

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:54.849
show and hide click off that and then

00:03:54.939 --> 00:04:05.689
insert another section brick next page

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:07.759
from the layout tab this third page can

00:04:05.689 --> 00:04:09.349
then be changed again so for example I

00:04:07.759 --> 00:04:12.250
could go back to poetry at fallout one

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:15.439
so as you can see I can have one page in

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.820
portrait one page in landscape and then

00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:20.239
when I wish to continue with the

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:22.280
document I can have the third page back

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:24.590
in

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:26.719
another tool that you may find useful is

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:29.479
that you may present information in

00:04:26.719 --> 00:04:31.849
column format so wrong having the text

00:04:29.479 --> 00:04:33.620
spread all across the page you may have

00:04:31.849 --> 00:04:35.360
a document where you need to insert it

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:37.580
in column format so if I place the

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.889
cursor at the front of the text on the

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.960
first page and if I look at the columns

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:45.259
button I click on that I can change it

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.849
to one to three columns so just as an

00:04:45.259 --> 00:04:49.340
example I'll change that to two columns

00:04:46.849 --> 00:04:51.169
as you can see all of the text has now

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:53.840
been bunched up on the left-hand side of

00:04:51.169 --> 00:04:56.599
the page if I just insert the clears are

00:04:53.840 --> 00:05:00.379
there and press the Enter key as you can

00:04:56.599 --> 00:05:03.620
see it is now moving the text to another

00:05:00.379 --> 00:05:05.060
column on the same page this can be

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:10.340
useful if you're presenting something

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:12.409
such as a newsletter as your document

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:14.180
increases in size it would be useful to

00:05:12.409 --> 00:05:19.669
insert page numbers so you can identify

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:22.520
the pages as a document across to do

00:05:19.669 --> 00:05:25.129
this we need to go to the insert tab so

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.750
I click on insert and as you can see I

00:05:25.129 --> 00:05:29.150
look along to the header and footer

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:31.879
section there's the option to insert

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:33.740
page numbers so I click on the page

00:05:31.879 --> 00:05:35.270
number and it will ask me if I wish to

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:37.759
place it at the top of the pH at the

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:39.589
bottom of the page in the margin of the

00:05:37.759 --> 00:05:41.270
page for this one I'm just going to

00:05:39.589 --> 00:05:42.699
select the bottom of the page and as you

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.889
can see there are a variety of

00:05:42.699 --> 00:05:47.509
formatting that can be applied to the

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:49.610
way the page number is entered for this

00:05:47.509 --> 00:05:52.849
one I'm going to simply select plain

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:54.710
number two and that will insert a page

00:05:52.849 --> 00:05:56.149
number in the footer section of the

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:58.039
document so I'll just click away from

00:05:56.149 --> 00:06:00.319
that and as you can see that is

00:05:58.039 --> 00:06:04.750
automatically inserted page numbers on

00:06:00.319 --> 00:06:04.750
the three pages within this document